{
  "dom_id": "step-613466",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding the Volume of a Solid When a Region is Enclosed Between Two Curves",
  "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded between the curves $y=3x-x^2$ and $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x^2.$ Calculate the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi$ radians about the $y$-axis.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let $f(x)=3x-x^2$ and $g(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2}x^2.$ \n\nWe start by determining the points where the curves intersect by solving the following equation for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =g(x) \\\\ 3x-{x}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2} \\\\ 3x-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x(2-x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=0$ and $x=2.$ So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2.$ \n\nNow, let's draw our usual vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower and upper functions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14224770/assets/5a9fd40682646575ada14297ef7e1de766852f99dbdab986d5baa1fb5c2feb94.png)\n\nThe vertical arrow \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=g(x)=\\dfrac12 x^2,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=f(x)=3x-x^2.$\n\nTherefore, using the shell method, the volume of the solid can be calculated as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{a}^{b}x([\\text{upper}]-[\\text{lower}])\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x([3x-{x}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}])\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x(3x-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x(x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x(\\frac{2x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x(2x-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\pi {(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\pi [(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{16}{4})-0] \\\\  & =4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-613466\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"613466\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"8854\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-613466\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-6\">Finding the Volume of a Solid When a Region is Enclosed Between Two Curves</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"613466\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            